# Line endings.
#
# Windows installs ship `core.autocrlf=true` in the system gitconfig, which
# rewrites checked-out files to CRLF. For a shell script that is fatal rather
# than cosmetic: `#!/bin/sh` followed by a carriage return is read as an
# interpreter named "sh\r", and every hook in .githooks/ dies with a "bad
# interpreter" error the moment someone clones on Windows. The hooks are what
# keep tool attribution out of commits, so they have to survive a clone.
#
# CI on ubuntu never sees the problem, which is exactly why it needs pinning
# here instead of being left to whoever notices first.

* text=auto eol=lf

.githooks/commit-msg text eol=lf
.githooks/pre-push   text eol=lf
*.sh                 text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
